{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:bb38326f7db1a023","name":"Heavy Fog","source":{"id":"source:reference-bb38326f7db1a023","title":"Heavy Fog","revision":21338,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:36:53Z","sha256":"3cc961e3a1d260e7fc9f9fd319ca711b43ff54c3af4c934a6477ef10b80eac97","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21338","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Heavy%20Fog&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-bb38326f7db1a023","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Thick fog covers the surface of ",{"tag":"a","children":["O'reen"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/O%27reen","referenceId":"reference:218e3e8c43c9574a"},", providing a good place for criminals to hide but also concealing the towering stone structures from those who ply the mist."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Much of the ground level of ",{"tag":"a","children":["O'reen"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/O%27reen","referenceId":"reference:218e3e8c43c9574a"}," is covered in a perpetual heavy fog. Most ",{"tag":"a","children":["O'reenian"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/O%27reenian","referenceId":"reference:abb7214e789a9b01"}," cities are built atop tall mesas and plateaus, meaning that most travelers don't have to deal with the Heavy Fog. However, the few, rare criminals on ",{"tag":"a","children":["O'reen"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/O%27reen","referenceId":"reference:218e3e8c43c9574a"}," often fly their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," through the Heavy Fog, staying below visual range and navigating by sensors alone. The practice is dangerous, and more than a few ships have had deadly collisions with the towering mesas.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Heavy Fog Statistics (CL 12)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Atmosphere"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Atmosphere"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A Starship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," end his or her turn within a square filled by Heavy Fog\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +14 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," As ",{"tag":"a","children":["Collision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Collision"}," with Colossal (Cruiser)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," On Trigger\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," (DC 31):"]}," A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"}," can use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," skill to give the Starship a +2 dodge bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," against this Hazard, warning the pilot about getting too close to a rock formation."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," (DC 26):"]}," As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"},", the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," can make a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Avoid Collision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Avoid_Collision"},". A successful check causes the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," to take half damage from the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Collision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Collision"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," (DC 21):"]}," As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},", the character can use the ship's sensors to try and pierce the fog and find a safe route around the jutting plateaus. Success grants a +5 circumstance bonus to the Starship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," against the Hazard's attacks."]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
